{
  "an8.51:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 8.51 ",
  "an8.51:0.2": "6. Gotamī ",
  "an8.51:0.3": "With Gotamī ",
  "an8.51:1.1": "At one time the Buddha was staying in the land of the Sakyans, near Kapilavatthu in the Banyan Tree Monastery. ",
  "an8.51:1.2": "Then Mahāpajāpati Gotamī went up to the Buddha, bowed, stood to one side, and said to him: ",
  "an8.51:1.3": "“Sir, please let ladies gain the going forth from the lay life to homelessness in the teaching and training proclaimed by the Realized One.” ",
  "an8.51:1.4": "“Enough, Gotamī. ",
  "an8.51:1.5": "Don’t endorse the going forth for ladies from the lay life to homelessness in the teaching and training proclaimed by the Realized One.” ",
  "an8.51:2.1": "For a second time … ",
  "an8.51:2.2": "",
  "an8.51:2.3": "",
  "an8.51:2.4": "",
  "an8.51:3.1": "For a third time, Mahāpajāpati Gotamī said to the Buddha: ",
  "an8.51:3.2": "“Sir, please let ladies gain the going forth from the lay life to homelessness in the teaching and training proclaimed by the Realized One.” ",
  "an8.51:3.3": "“Enough, Gotamī. ",
  "an8.51:3.4": "Don’t endorse the going forth for ladies from the lay life to homelessness in the teaching and training proclaimed by the Realized One.” ",
  "an8.51:4.1": "Then Mahāpajāpati Gotamī thought, “The Buddha does not permit ladies to go forth.” Miserable and sad, weeping, with a tearful face, she bowed, and respectfully circled the Buddha, keeping him on her right, before leaving. ",
  "an8.51:5.1": 